codex
K does not persist proved claims as lemmas across `kprove` runs, so the entry proof cannot directly reuse the already-proved loop theorem. I’m applying the contract’s staged bridge pattern: prove membership bridge-free, compile that exact theorem as a bridge to prove the loop, then compile the exact loop theorem as a tightly matched bridge for the entry. Each bridge’s match domain will be identical to its prior machine-checked claim, and each claim will be rerun against a definition that does not contain its own bridge.
apply patch
patch: completed
